    "faq_group_iCKDei": {
      "type": "faq-group",
      "blocks": {
        "question_y4bdrm": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "What warranty comes with my NMJ jewellery?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What warranty comes with my NMJ jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>Our jewellery is thoughtfully made to be loved and worn, and we stand behind the quality of our craftsmanship.</p><p>Fine jewellery is covered by a 12 month manufacturer’s warranty from the original purchase date for eligible manufacturing and craftsmanship faults.</p><p>Engagement and Bespoke pieces have a limited lifetime manufacturer’s warranty covering eligible manufacturing and craftsmanship faults, subject to our Terms.</p><p>Please see our Warranty Guide for more information.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_qNRfxW": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Can you repair my jewellery outside the warranty period?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you repair my jewellery outside the warranty period?",
            "answer": "<p>We are committed to helping you care for your NMJ jewellery throughout its lifetime.</p><p>Where reasonably possible, we will assess an NMJ piece for repair outside its warranty period. Fees may apply, and repair suitability will depend on the condition of the piece, the work required and the availability of suitable materials and components.</p><p>Not every piece can be repaired. If a repair is not reasonably possible, our team may discuss alternative options with you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_W3MeQX": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Can you repair jewellery made by another jeweller?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you repair jewellery made by another jeweller?",
            "answer": "<p>To ensure we can confidently care for the quality and integrity of every piece we work with, our repair and servicing services are reserved for jewellery purchased from NMJ.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_w6jRGt": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Can you replace a missing stone, earring back or other component?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you replace a missing stone, earring back or other component?",
            "answer": "<p>Where possible, we can replace missing stones, earring backs and other components for NMJ pieces. Please contact our Customer Service team or bring your piece into one of our showrooms so we can assess what is required.</p><p>Replacement options are subject to the availability of suitable stones and components. Our team will confirm the available options, cost and estimated timeframe before proceeding.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_CxRgg4": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Do you offer resizing, cleaning, refurbishment and rhodium-plating services?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer resizing, cleaning, refurbishment and rhodium-plating services?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We offer professional servicing and rhodium plating to help restore and maintain your jewellery.</p><p>Eligible Engagement and Bespoke pieces receive complimentary lifetime routine servicing. This includes:</p><p>A thorough inspection;</p><p>Professional cleaning and polishing;</p><p>Assessment of stones, settings, claws and band; and</p><p>Routine tightening where required and reasonably possible.</p><p>Repairs, replacement stones, restoration, resizing and replacement components fall outside routine servicing and may incur an additional cost. We will always discuss any recommended work and associated costs with you before proceeding.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_emFyF3": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  How do I send or deliver my jewellery to you for assessment or servicing?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I send or deliver my jewellery to you for assessment or servicing?",
            "answer": "<p>Please contact our Customer Service team before sending your piece so we can guide you through the process.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_aawCwX": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  How long will my repair or service take?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long will my repair or service take?",
            "answer": "<p>An estimated timeframe will be provided alongside your repair or service quotation. This timeframe is a guide only, as the full extent of the work required may not become apparent until our jewellers begin working on your piece.</p><p>If we find that additional time or further work is needed, our Customer Service team will be in touch to discuss this with you and provide an updated timeframe.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ihePFq": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "How should I care for and store my jewellery?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I care for and store my jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>To keep your jewellery looking its best, we recommend removing it before washing your hands, showering, swimming, exercising or sleeping. Soap, natural skin oils and other residue can collect beneath settings and between fine chain links, attracting dirt and causing your piece to become dull more quickly.</p><p>Jewellery should also be removed before applying creams, lotions, perfumes and other beauty products, as these can leave a sticky residue on the metal and stones.</p><p>When not being worn, store each piece separately in a clean, dry place or soft jewellery pouch to help protect it from moisture, tarnishing, scratching or tangling. Our signature NMJ boxes are designed for presentation rather than long-term storage, as the adhesives used within jewellery boxes may react with precious metals over time and contribute to tarnishing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_RAEkYz": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "How often should I clean my jewellery at home?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How often should I clean my jewellery at home?",
            "answer": "<p>For pieces worn regularly, we recommend a gentle at-home clean every few weeks, or whenever you notice a build-up of oils, lotions or everyday residue. Lightly wiping your jewellery with a soft, lint-free cloth after wear can also help maintain its finish between cleans.</p><p>The most suitable cleaning method will depend on the metal, stones and construction of your piece, as some gemstones require more delicate care. Always refer to our Care Guide for instructions on cleaning your particular piece, and if you are unsure, contact our Customer Service team before cleaning it at home.</p><p></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_BTtEGN": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "How often should my jewellery be professionally serviced?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How often should my jewellery be professionally serviced?",
            "answer": "<p>We recommend having stone-set jewellery professionally inspected and serviced every 12 months. Regular servicing allows our jewellers to check the settings, claws and overall condition of your piece, helping to identify signs of wear before they develop into more significant issues.</p><p>We offer a complimentary annual clean and service for all NMJ bespoke and online engagement pieces. Please contact our Customer Service team or visit one of our showrooms to arrange your service.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_mWBXJQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Which stones require additional care or should not be cleaned at home?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which stones require additional care or should not be cleaned at home?",
            "answer": "<p>Delicate, porous or heavily included stones require additional care. This includes our Sashi and Sana pieces, pearls, opals, emerald, turquoise, lapis lazuli, coral and amber. These stones can be sensitive to moisture, heat, chemicals, sudden temperature changes and vigorous cleaning.</p><p>Avoid placing these pieces in ultrasonic or steam cleaners, soaking them in water or using household cleaners, detergents and abrasive cloths. Instead, gently wipe them with a clean, soft, slightly damp cloth and allow them to dry completely before storing.</p><p>If you are unsure how to care for a particular stone or product, please contact our Customer Care team before cleaning it at home. We will be happy to advise on the safest method of your piece.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_V3DCbQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Why has my jewellery tarnished, and how can I help prevent it?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why has my jewellery tarnished, and how can I help prevent it?",
            "answer": "<p>Tarnishing is a natural surface reaction that can occur when precious metals are exposed to air, moisture, natural skin oils, chemicals and environmental elements. It is particularly common with sterling silver but may also appear on gold alloys over time. Tarnishing does not mean your jewellery is faulty and can generally be removed through appropriate cleaning or professional servicing.</p><p>To help minimise tarnishing, remove your jewellery before showering, swimming, exercising or applying perfumes, lotions and cleaning products. After wearing, gently wipe each piece with a soft, lint-free cloth and store it separately in a clean, dry jewellery pouch.</p><p>Our signature NMJ boxes are intended for presentation rather than long-term storage, as adhesives used within jewellery boxes may react with precious metals over time and contribute to tarnishing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_dmz84L": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Do you recommend insuring my jewellery?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you recommend insuring my jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, we strongly recommend arranging comprehensive insurance for your jewellery, particularly engagement rings, bespoke pieces and other precious or frequently worn designs. While our warranty covers eligible manufacturing faults, it does not cover loss, theft or accidental damage.</p><p>We recommend confirming the level of protection offered, including whether your policy provides cover while travelling when your jewellery is worn outside the home.</p><p>Our team can support with setting up an interim policy for you upon collection of your piece.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
