    "faq_group_eTtDmY": {
      "type": "faq-group",
      "blocks": {
        "question_TfRAtT": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": " What is your bespoke service, and how does the process work? ",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is your bespoke service, and how does the process work?",
            "answer": "<p>Our bespoke service is a deeply personal design experience, allowing you to create a piece that is thoughtfully tailored to your story, style and vision.</p><p>You will be paired with a dedicated bespoke designer, beginning with an initial discovery call to explore your ideas, preferences, budget and timeframe. From there, your designer will source suitable stones and share initial design concepts and quotations for your consideration.</p><p>Where relevant, you will be invited to a private stone viewing with your designer before receiving detailed sketches or renders of your piece to review and approve. Once the final design has been confirmed and your deposit has been paid, your piece will move into production, where it will be carefully brought to life by our skilled team.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ajtaT6": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  How long does the bespoke process take?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the bespoke process take?",
            "answer": "<p>The timeframe for your bespoke journey will vary depending on the complexity of your design, the number of stones you would like to consider and the time required to source the perfect option.</p><p>Particularly rare or specialised stones may take longer to locate, while additional rounds of design refinements may also extend the process. Your bespoke designer will keep you informed throughout each stage and provide an estimated timeframe based on the unique requirements of your piece.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_RV6Qww": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "How much does a bespoke piece cost, and is there a minimum spend?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does a bespoke piece cost, and is there a minimum spend?",
            "answer": "<p>There is no minimum spend for our bespoke service. Each piece is individually quoted based on its unique design, including the precious metal, stone selection, complexity and craftsmanship involved.</p><p>Following your initial discovery call or appointment, your designer will share initial concepts and quotations for your consideration. Any design decisions or refinements that may affect the price will be discussed with you throughout the process before the final design is approved.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_QeYcGP": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  What deposit is required, and can I pay in instalments?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What deposit is required, and can I pay in instalments?",
            "answer": "<p>Payment for your bespoke piece is made in two stages. A 50-75% deposit is required before production begins, allowing us to secure your selected materials and commence crafting your piece. The remaining balance is due once your piece is complete and before it is dispatched or collected.</p><p>Your bespoke designer will keep you informed throughout the process and provide payment instructions at each stage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_bcpXF9": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  How do you source stones for bespoke pieces?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do you source stones for bespoke pieces?",
            "answer": "<p>We work with a trusted network of carefully selected stone suppliers who meet our due diligence requirements for responsible sourcing and business practices.</p><p>During your initial discovery call or appointment, your bespoke designer will take the time to understand your preferences, including stone type, shape, colour, size, quality and budget. They will then thoughtfully source a selection of stones that best reflect your vision for you to consider.</p><p>The sourcing timeframe will vary depending on your requirements, as particularly rare or specialised stones may take longer to find.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Dxd7RK": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Will I approve the design before production begins?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I approve the design before production begins?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Before your piece enters production, your bespoke designer will provide sketches, digital renders or reference imagery for you to review.</p><p>You will have the opportunity to discuss the design, request any final refinements and confirm that you are happy with each detail. Production will only begin once you have approved the final design and paid your deposit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_xaWJ8k": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Do you create bespoke pieces other than engagement rings?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you create bespoke pieces other than engagement rings?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, our bespoke service extends beyond engagement rings to a variety of meaningful, one-of-a-kind pieces.</p><p>We recommend exploring our bespoke archive to discover examples of previous commissions and gain a sense of what may be possible. If you have a particular idea in mind, please contact our Customer Care team, who can discuss your vision and guide you through the next steps.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_A3V6Wf": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  Do you work with customer-supplied or heirloom stones?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you work with customer-supplied or heirloom stones?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, we may be able to incorporate customer-supplied or heirloom stones into a bespoke piece on a case-by-case basis.</p><p>Before confirming whether we can work with your stone, our team will need to assess its condition, dimensions and suitability for the proposed design. As older stones may have existing wear, damage or unique setting requirements, not every stone will be suitable for resetting.</p><p>Please contact our Customer Care team with details and imagery of your stone, and they will guide you through the assessment process and available options</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_WaKp7p": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "What options are available if I do not have time to complete the bespoke process?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What options are available if I do not have time to complete the bespoke process?",
            "answer": "<p>If your proposal date is approaching and there is not enough time to complete the full bespoke process, we may be able to arrange a temporary proposal ring, such as our Promise Ring.</p><p>This allows you to propose with a beautiful piece while giving you and your partner the opportunity to begin the bespoke journey together afterward. You can then collaborate with one of our dedicated bespoke designers to create an engagement ring that thoughtfully reflects your shared vision.</p><p>We also stock a selection of ‘ready to wear’ engagement styles in our boutiques and online which can be purchased for immediate dispatch.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_jaxYqb": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "How long is a bespoke quote valid?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long is a bespoke quote valid?",
            "answer": "<p>Bespoke quotations are valid for 14 days from the date of issue. As precious metal and gemstone prices fluctuate, any quotation accepted after this period may need to be reviewed and updated.</p><p>Please note that quoted stones are subject to availability and are not secured until your deposit has been received. If your preferred stone is no longer available, your bespoke designer will source a comparable alternative for your consideration and provide an updated quotation where required.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_EWrmR7": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "  What warranty, resizing and servicing are included with a bespoke piece?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What warranty, resizing and servicing are included with a bespoke piece?",
            "answer": "<p>Our bespoke pieces are accompanied by a limited lifetime manufacturing warranty, subject to the piece being returned to NMJ for its complimentary annual clean, inspection and service. This allows our jewellers to assess the settings, claws and overall condition of your piece and identify signs of wear before they develop into more significant concerns.</p><p>Bespoke engagement and ceremonial rings also include one complimentary resize within six months of receiving your piece, where the design allows. Some styles, stone settings and significant size adjustments may not be suitable for resizing, and our team will assess this on a case-by-case basis.</p><p>Our warranty covers eligible manufacturing faults but does not extend to accidental damage, loss, theft, general wear and tear or work completed by another jeweller. We recommend arranging comprehensive insurance to protect your piece once it has been received.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_aJgphh": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Where should I have my bespoke piece cleaned and serviced?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where should I have my bespoke piece cleaned and serviced?",
            "answer": "<p>Your bespoke piece should be returned to Natalie Marie Jewellery for its complimentary annual clean, inspection and service. This allows our jewellers to carefully assess the settings, claws and overall condition of your piece, while ensuring any servicing is completed in accordance with its original design and craftsmanship.</p><p>Annual servicing by NMJ is required to maintain the validity of your limited lifetime manufacturing warranty. Please contact our Customer Care team or bring your piece into either of our showrooms to arrange your service. We recommend that repairs, resizing or alterations are not undertaken by another jeweller, as third-party work may affect your warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_cPz6LA": {
          "type": "question",
          "name": "Do you work with interstate and international clients?",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you work with interstate and international clients?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, we work with clients across Australia and around the world. Your bespoke journey can be facilitated remotely through video appointments, phone calls and email, allowing you to collaborate closely with your designer at each stage of the process.</p><p>Once complete, your bespoke piece can be securely shipped interstate or internationally. International clients should refer to our Shipping and Duties & Taxes Terms and Conditions for information regarding delivery, customs requirements and any applicable import duties or taxes.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
